When I first solved “Move Zeroes”, I didn’t struggle with the code — This article explains: What I tried The exact idea behind read and write pointers How the algorithm works step by step The pattern I learned from this problem Problem Summary You are given an array of integers nums.Move all 0s to the end of the array without changing the relative order of non-zero elements. Note:You must do this in-place. Example Input: [0,1,0,3,12] Output: [1,3,12,0,0]
Key intuition Instead of searching for zeros, Once non-zero values are placed in front, This problem uses a two-pointer pattern: rd → read pointer (scans the array) wrt → write pointer (marks where the next non-zero should go) class Solution { public: void moveZeroes(vector<int>& nums) { int wrt = 0, rd = 0;
